# cella.policy for build-pmars (titanium-owned: the task is vendored).
# The task builds pMARS from Debian source packages, so it fetches from
# the apt mirror over plain HTTP. Collected once with DRY_RUN=true, then
# reviewed: only the world name is kept -- the appliance's own infra
# (upstream DNS, the reply window, ARP) is composed by titanium, not
# declared here. The window keeps the flow live instead of freezing.
release outgoing deb.debian.org:80/tcp (keep_open=60m) (skip_freeze=true)
release incoming deb.debian.org:80/tcp
